Access an array item by its index

This example shows how to access items in the fruits array by specifying the index number of their position in the array.

const fruits = ["Apple", "Banana"];

// The index of an array's first element is always 0.
fruits[0]; // Apple

// The index of an array's sec

Closure

Consider the following code example:

function makeFunc() {
  const name = "Mozilla";
  function displayName() {
    console.log(name);
  }
  return displayName;
}

const myFunc = makeFunc();
myFunc();

Running this code has exactly the same effect as the previous example of the init() func

